WEBVTT

00:00:58.000 --> 00:01:01.030
<b>Skull-face Bookseller Honda-san</b>

00:01:01.700 --> 00:01:08.040
<b>Bookstores are so Wonderful!</b>

00:01:02.210 --> 00:01:06.850
<i>Why do people buy books at bookstores?</i>

00:01:08.550 --> 00:01:10.280
<i>88...</i>

00:01:10.790 --> 00:01:12.300
<i>89...</i>

00:01:13.350 --> 00:01:14.970
<i>90 books!</i>

00:01:15.720 --> 00:01:21.530
Uh, if you'd like, we also do deliveries.

00:01:16.850 --> 00:01:21.860
<b>That's a ton of books!</b>

00:01:22.080 --> 00:01:23.220
Uh...

00:01:23.990 --> 00:01:26.730
I have to bring them home today.

00:01:26.330 --> 00:01:28.260
<b>Dead eyes!!</b>

00:01:28.430 --> 00:01:29.320
Shipping?

00:01:29.320 --> 00:01:31.330
No, he's taking it home.

00:01:31.580 --> 00:01:33.000
Maybe three bags?

00:01:33.140 --> 00:01:34.640
I'll take the slips out.

00:01:34.640 --> 00:01:36.870
And off go the helpers

00:01:34.980 --> 00:01:36.720
Thank you.

00:01:36.720 --> 00:01:38.450
Thank you for waiting.

00:01:38.450 --> 00:01:39.900
I'll carry these to the door.

00:01:39.900 --> 00:01:42.310
Huh? Oh no, it's fine.

00:01:42.310 --> 00:01:45.850
I can take one in my backpack 
and carry the other two.

00:01:51.910 --> 00:01:53.350
He could have bought them online.

00:01:55.240 --> 00:01:58.220
That's a terrible, horrible, 
no good, very bad thing to say!

00:01:58.220 --> 00:02:00.160
I mean, it's convenient.

00:02:00.580 --> 00:02:03.740
Besides, there's people who like <i>books</i>, 
then there's people who like book<i>stores</i>.

00:02:04.070 --> 00:02:06.940
I buy online when I have way
 too many books to get.

00:02:06.940 --> 00:02:08.230
It's easier.

00:02:08.230 --> 00:02:09.830
She's so right, it kills me!

00:02:10.870 --> 00:02:13.210
<b>Foreign Comics</b>

00:02:11.780 --> 00:02:13.210
<i>It's true.</i>

00:02:13.540 --> 00:02:17.550
<i>Maybe book lovers and bookstore lovers</i>

00:02:17.550 --> 00:02:21.220
<i>are endangered species.</i>

00:02:22.230 --> 00:02:24.340
Pardon me.

00:02:25.630 --> 00:02:28.860
I've been asked to buy 
a book, but I can't find it.

00:02:28.860 --> 00:02:32.270
I'd really appreciate if 
you could help me out.

00:02:32.270 --> 00:02:33.690
Sure thing.

00:02:33.860 --> 00:02:35.720
I can look it up and bring it up for you.

00:02:35.720 --> 00:02:38.110
Really? Thanks.

00:02:41.250 --> 00:02:42.150
<i>H...</i>

00:02:43.220 --> 00:02:47.040
<i>His finger!</i>

00:02:45.170 --> 00:02:47.040
<b>Not an artistic error!</b>

00:02:47.450 --> 00:02:50.100
<i>Nah, hold up, Honda.</i>

00:02:50.100 --> 00:02:52.550
<i>Get a grip, you goddamn wuss.</i>

00:02:52.760 --> 00:02:56.630
<i>So what if he's missin' a finger or two?</i>

00:02:56.630 --> 00:03:00.290
<i>It doesn't mean he can't buy
 a freakin' book at a bookstore.</i>

00:02:57.480 --> 00:03:00.290
<b>We got stock, yo.</b>

00:03:00.530 --> 00:03:05.860
<i>Forget it. No way you can let yourself be
 a rude-ass to your customers, Honda.</i>

00:03:08.050 --> 00:03:11.270
Th-Th-Thanks f-for wait...

00:03:09.830 --> 00:03:12.350
Hey, that was fast.

00:03:12.840 --> 00:03:16.090
Okay, that's the one. Yup.

00:03:16.090 --> 00:03:18.700
I want you to ship them for me.

00:03:18.850 --> 00:03:21.850
We'll have to ask for a shipping charge.

00:03:21.850 --> 00:03:23.360
Sure, okay.

00:03:23.360 --> 00:03:25.680
Not a problem.

00:03:27.320 --> 00:03:33.260
Man, they said they wanted to come buy it 
themselves instead of sendin' a proxy,

00:03:33.260 --> 00:03:35.090
but that just ain't an option right now.

00:03:36.260 --> 00:03:40.830
They won't shut up about wanting 
to come book shopping by themselves.

00:03:41.120 --> 00:03:44.660
They said just being in a 
bookstore makes 'em happy.

00:03:46.260 --> 00:03:48.660
We'll be waiting.

00:03:48.660 --> 00:03:51.340
Okay, I'll let them know.

00:03:51.760 --> 00:03:53.640
See ya later, Honda-san.

00:03:54.310 --> 00:03:55.840
I'm countin' on you.

00:03:58.680 --> 00:04:02.210
<b>thump thump thump</b>

00:03:58.880 --> 00:04:02.210
<b>(Palpitation)</b>

00:03:59.200 --> 00:04:01.880
<i>How does he know my name?!</i>

00:04:01.880 --> 00:04:03.470
<i>Oh, right. My name tag.</i>

00:04:03.470 --> 00:04:06.080
<i>Just kill me, please.</i>

00:04:06.510 --> 00:04:07.470
Lantern-san.

00:04:07.470 --> 00:04:08.310
Yeah?

00:04:08.930 --> 00:04:11.210
Could you check this shipment?

00:04:11.210 --> 00:04:12.520
Yep.

00:04:13.480 --> 00:04:16.720
Oh, this is headed for a prison.

00:04:17.590 --> 00:04:21.760
Books can be ordered to prisons, too! 
A lot of places don't even need you
 to write the name of the prison!

00:04:17.890 --> 00:04:19.820
<i>Okay, I'll let them know.</i>

00:04:19.820 --> 00:04:22.050
<i>Okay. No problem.</i>

00:04:22.050 --> 00:04:23.370
<i>Okay.</i>

00:04:22.990 --> 00:04:25.600
<i>Mister Okay!</i>

00:04:23.370 --> 00:04:25.600
<i>Okay.</i>

00:04:27.510 --> 00:04:31.230
<i>We get all kinds of customers daily.</i>

00:04:32.540 --> 00:04:36.510
<i>A bookstore is simply a means 
by which one can acquire books.</i>

00:04:36.510 --> 00:04:40.220
<i>There are all kinds of reasons 
that they travel here.</i>

00:04:42.510 --> 00:04:46.700
<i>They said just being in a 
bookstore makes them happy.</i>

00:04:47.830 --> 00:04:52.030
<i>I mean, I appreciate it, but I think 
that's a pretty rare kind of person.</i>

00:04:49.860 --> 00:04:53.250
<b>Rare</b>

00:04:52.030 --> 00:04:53.380
Hello.

00:04:53.380 --> 00:04:54.130
Yes?

00:04:55.300 --> 00:04:57.730
I'd like to buy these.

00:04:57.730 --> 00:05:00.160
That looks scary.

00:04:57.730 --> 00:05:01.270
<b>thump thump thump</b>

00:05:00.160 --> 00:05:03.320
No dude, these are legit good.

00:05:00.330 --> 00:05:04.300
<i>Still, we should be very thankful</i>

00:05:03.320 --> 00:05:05.180
I swear, man.

00:05:04.300 --> 00:05:07.700
<i>that they chose to buy books from a bookstore.</i>

00:05:05.180 --> 00:05:08.250
Whoa, that's scary.

00:05:08.250 --> 00:05:09.690
Totally, fam.

00:05:09.690 --> 00:05:11.010
That's super funny.

00:05:11.010 --> 00:05:13.980
<b>The Shelves with and without Restrictions</b>

00:05:14.410 --> 00:05:19.150
<i>Some customers who don't speak my language, 
some that do but are way too odd...</i>

00:05:19.150 --> 00:05:21.990
<i>You'd think I'd have gotten used 
to service work by now, right?</i>

00:05:23.770 --> 00:05:26.360
<i>I do have more guts now,</i>

00:05:26.360 --> 00:05:30.500
<i>but there are still some customers that 
send my heart racing when I see them.</i>

00:05:31.470 --> 00:05:32.540
Specifically...

00:05:32.540 --> 00:05:33.530
Hello!

00:05:33.530 --> 00:05:34.430
Yes?

00:05:35.050 --> 00:05:36.590
This one, please!

00:05:36.590 --> 00:05:37.500
Please!

00:05:38.020 --> 00:05:39.230
<i>Kids!</i>

00:05:40.010 --> 00:05:42.380
429 yen + tax

00:05:40.010 --> 00:05:42.380
Price

00:05:43.780 --> 00:05:45.850
<b>Total: 463 yen</b>

00:05:43.780 --> 00:05:45.850
<b>*With tax included</b>

00:05:55.750 --> 00:05:58.700
Oh, my! I'm sorry, it does 
say "tax not included."

00:05:58.700 --> 00:06:00.000
Don't worry, we can buy it.

00:06:00.000 --> 00:06:00.890
I'm sorry.

00:06:00.890 --> 00:06:03.530
No, I'm sorry it's so confusing.

00:06:03.880 --> 00:06:04.500
Here.

00:06:04.500 --> 00:06:07.440
It's all yours now, ma'am.

00:06:08.220 --> 00:06:11.020
<i>So that just happened.</i>

00:06:11.890 --> 00:06:15.900
Doesn't it scare you when kids are around?

00:06:15.900 --> 00:06:16.650
Creepy.

00:06:16.650 --> 00:06:18.220
No, I mean...

00:06:18.480 --> 00:06:21.720
I'm always dead inside when 
I deal with customers,

00:06:18.480 --> 00:06:27.790
<b>Artist rendition</b>

00:06:22.050 --> 00:06:26.190
so when I'm confronted by 
their purity and honest eyes,

00:06:26.190 --> 00:06:27.790
I get flustered.

00:06:28.230 --> 00:06:32.330
I can't help but wonder if it's creepy

00:06:32.330 --> 00:06:34.890
if I look at them while thinking 
about how cute they are.

00:06:34.890 --> 00:06:36.010
<i>Definitely</i> creepy.

00:06:36.010 --> 00:06:37.870
Wait, when did you show up?

00:06:38.130 --> 00:06:40.820
I get that they can be 
distracting, but, like...

00:06:40.820 --> 00:06:44.790
I guess the picture book 
section has it rough.

00:06:45.700 --> 00:06:48.340
Well, I bet their purity 
causes a lot of incidents.

00:06:48.660 --> 00:06:51.140
Oh, actually, just the other day...

00:06:55.030 --> 00:06:56.400
Huh?

00:06:56.400 --> 00:06:58.230
Where is she?

00:06:58.720 --> 00:07:16.500
<b>Dreamy Transformations Fair</b>

00:07:00.940 --> 00:07:02.710
Found you, Mommy!

00:07:03.280 --> 00:07:04.740
Wh-Wh-What's wrong?

00:07:04.740 --> 00:07:06.390
You can't be here.

00:07:06.390 --> 00:07:08.450
Want to go back to Daddy?

00:07:08.450 --> 00:07:11.420
What's this? <i>*retty Cure</i>? Who's the man?

00:07:11.420 --> 00:07:13.130
Th-That's....

00:07:13.130 --> 00:07:14.470
The man is...

00:07:18.070 --> 00:07:20.400
No, no, no, wait, wait!

00:07:20.400 --> 00:07:21.770
Mom?

00:07:21.770 --> 00:07:25.130
Go any further, and you might 
never be able to come back!

00:07:25.130 --> 00:07:27.000
Huh? Why?

00:07:27.000 --> 00:07:29.020
Because I couldn't, either!

00:07:30.510 --> 00:07:33.920
There's so much drama around 
the super fetish-y shelves.

00:07:34.190 --> 00:07:36.830
Purity can be a sin at times.

00:07:36.830 --> 00:07:37.580
A sin.

00:07:38.000 --> 00:07:39.490
Purity...

00:07:45.110 --> 00:07:47.550
This girl's so adorable!

00:07:49.000 --> 00:07:50.100
Welcome!

00:07:50.100 --> 00:07:51.990
I can help you over here.

00:07:56.010 --> 00:07:58.670
But we just made eye contact!

00:07:58.670 --> 00:08:00.760
You might have scared her.

00:08:03.180 --> 00:08:03.820
Huh?

00:08:04.690 --> 00:08:06.000
Why are you...

00:08:06.000 --> 00:08:07.040
No...

00:08:06.480 --> 00:08:07.410
<b>Exit</b>

00:08:07.420 --> 00:08:14.460
<b>Exit</b>

00:08:07.420 --> 00:08:14.460
<b>Entrance</b>

00:08:07.970 --> 00:08:13.430
Is she going all the way around to the 
entrance because I'm at the exit side?

00:08:14.460 --> 00:08:16.100
This one, please!

00:08:17.330 --> 00:08:19.870
Such a good girl!

00:08:20.500 --> 00:08:21.560
Creepy.

00:08:21.560 --> 00:08:24.140
No, that's not—Well, it is, but...

00:08:24.140 --> 00:08:26.830
Tell Section Chief Armor, not me!

00:08:29.110 --> 00:08:30.160
<i>Honestly, though,</i>

00:08:30.700 --> 00:08:36.520
<i>it makes me really happy when I see customers
 picking up manga with sparkles in their eyes.</i>

00:08:37.480 --> 00:08:38.670
Pardon me.

00:08:38.670 --> 00:08:39.350
Yes?

00:08:39.650 --> 00:08:42.750
My dad and I love manga.

00:08:42.750 --> 00:08:44.830
We're here from Texas.

00:08:45.610 --> 00:08:47.040
Konnichiwa.

00:08:47.040 --> 00:08:49.420
Where can I find <i>Naru**</i>?

00:08:50.560 --> 00:08:52.030
<b>Shu-E-sha Shounen</b>

00:08:50.570 --> 00:08:52.030
Over here.

00:08:54.110 --> 00:08:56.030
<i>Such a reaction...</i>

00:08:56.490 --> 00:08:58.120
Fantastic...

00:08:58.120 --> 00:08:59.700
<i>Dad, you too?!</i>

00:09:00.800 --> 00:09:02.330
<i>Wow...</i>

00:09:02.330 --> 00:09:05.660
<i>I've never seen </i>Naru**<i> move people so much.</i>

00:09:06.080 --> 00:09:09.970
<i>I'm sure they sell it in Texas, 
but I probably shouldn't say that.</i>

00:09:14.070 --> 00:09:17.890
<i>Maybe there are no borders 
in the purity of love,</i>

00:09:17.890 --> 00:09:21.220
<i>regardless of age, sex, or nationality.</i>

00:09:22.150 --> 00:09:24.490
<b>Kame</b>

00:09:25.010 --> 00:09:28.030
<i>But they aren't all in on just </i>Naru**<i>, huh?</i>

00:09:31.000 --> 00:09:34.000
<b>Go for it, Azarashi san! 
~The Hidden Ambition~</b>

00:09:35.530 --> 00:09:38.000
<b>Skull-face Bookseller Honda-san</b>

00:09:35.530 --> 00:09:38.000
<b>Open to live action adaptation offers!</b>

00:09:35.530 --> 00:09:38.000
<b>I'll be waiting for your call ❤</b>

00:09:36.720 --> 00:09:41.770
Honda-san, I have faith that <i>Skull-face</i> 
can get a live action adaptation.

00:09:41.770 --> 00:09:45.380
I want more people to
 experience such a good work.

00:09:45.380 --> 00:09:50.950
Keep the original plot, and you could 
be played by a hot actor just fine.

00:09:51.160 --> 00:09:51.880
Honda!

00:09:51.880 --> 00:09:53.560
Here's your new face!

00:09:55.030 --> 00:09:56.930
I was about to wet myself.

00:09:57.360 --> 00:09:58.660
You want <i>just</i> the bonuses?

00:09:58.660 --> 00:10:00.090
I see, I understand.

00:10:00.090 --> 00:10:01.030
No can do!

00:10:01.030 --> 00:10:03.260
Welcome!

00:10:03.260 --> 00:10:04.800
Muscles and muscles!

00:10:04.800 --> 00:10:07.200
This muscley guy is the <i>uke</i>!

00:10:07.630 --> 00:10:09.210
I see.

00:10:09.210 --> 00:10:09.740
See?

00:10:09.740 --> 00:10:11.840
Doesn't that get you pumped?

00:10:11.840 --> 00:10:16.310
No, but even if he were a hot guy, 
he'd still have my personality!

00:10:16.490 --> 00:10:19.930
Nah. If he's hot, he could get 
away with that personality.

00:10:19.930 --> 00:10:21.420
Right, Chief Editor?

00:10:21.420 --> 00:10:22.360
Sure.

00:10:22.360 --> 00:10:25.970
Also, could you draw me as a koala?

00:10:26.490 --> 00:10:28.170
<i>What is this, a zoo?</i>
